  "Tweed Water Spaniel": "The Tweed Water Spaniel was a Borders water-working dog used for retrieving in rivers and rough country. Its reconstructed ancestry combines water-spaniel stock with St John's Water Dog influence. The type disappeared, but its importance survives through the Golden Retriever and later Goldendoodle line.",
  "Water spaniel and Collie": "Water spaniel and Collie denotes mixed working influence between water-retrieving dogs and pastoral collie stock in later retriever or farm-dog development.",
